#import "../helpers/shared.typ": req, budget, src, supply, pitfall
= Milestones, Timeline, and Evaluation Plan <sec-milestones>
#budget(0.8, 480)

#req(source: "SOL §VI.A — Track 1 criterion 4")[
Does the proposal present a specific, actionable list of milestones and evaluation plan?
]

#pitfall(source: "DECK, 'Strengthen Submission'")[
"Be specific in your planning and evaluation, use actionable list of milestones. These
should cover all components, *beyond just the cyber technology.*"
]

#src("W1", "@ 00:41:38")[
"Be very specific about what your milestones are and your evaluation plan to assess where
you are and the progress of your work."
]

#src("W2", "video_summary — Team Size and Justification")[
Milestones should carry justified numeric targets. NSF's example of the reasoning it
expects: why a 5%, 10%, or 50% community growth figure is the right one for this project,
and whether the team is sized to deliver it.
]

#supply[
- Quarterly milestone table over 12 months. Tables may use a smaller font.
- Per milestone: named deliverable + completion condition an external reviewer can verify
- Coverage across *all* workstreams — governance, community, security, sustainability —
  not only technical items
- Evaluation indicators with targets set against the §2 baseline, not in the abstract
- Suggested quarterly centers of gravity:
  + Q1 — I-Corps kickoff; interview instrument; baseline metrics; audits initiated
  + Q2 — bulk interviews; governance model survey; threat model draft
  + Q3 — interviews complete + synthesized; model selected; charter + security plan drafts
  + Q4 — cost/revenue model; host-structure recommendation; consolidated plan; I-Corps close
]
